      <item id="14">
        <title>
          <en>Moonlight in the City × Vivir Mi Vida</en>
          <zh>《城里的月光 × Vivir Mi Vida》</zh>
        </title>
        <genre>
          <en>Cross-Cultural Instrumental Fusion</en>
          <zh>跨文化器乐融合</zh>
        </genre>
        <performers>
          <performer>
            <name>
              <en>Dr. Fang Shu (Fang Music)</en>
              <zh>舒放博士</zh>
            </name>
            <bio>
              <en>Scholar, multi-instrumentalist, and cultural visionary Dr. Fang Shu bridges academic rigor with ancestral resonance. An Associate Teaching Professor at Florida International University, he is also the founder of FANG MUSIC, an artistic initiative dedicated to re-imagining the ancient Chinese ruan (moon lute) for modern, global stages. Merging millennium-old traditional idioms with contemporary sonic palettes, Dr. Shu introduces audiences worldwide to the expressive power and depth of Chinese heritage.</en>
              <zh>学者、器乐演奏家与文化探索者。舒方博士现任佛罗里达国际大学（FIU）副教学教授；在学术之外，他创立“FANG MUSIC”，致力于将中国传统弹拨乐器——中阮，带入现代国际音乐语境。他将跨越千年的古典韵律与当代先锋声景精妙交融，以独具张力的当代诠释向全球观众呈现中国民乐的深邃意境与时代生命力。</zh>
            </bio>
          </performer>
          <performer>
            <name>
              <en>Joel Fabelo (Joel Indira Band)</en>
              <zh>乔尔·法贝洛</zh>
            </name>
            <bio>
              <en>Cuban flutist and master educator Joel Fabelo brings more than two decades of international concert and orchestral artistry to the stage. Renowned for his fluid virtuosity, Fabelo moves effortlessly between rigorous classical repertoire and vibrant Afro-Cuban traditions. A versatile soloist and chamber artist across the Americas, he currently leads Miami’s premier Latin ensembles while shaping the next generation of woodwind performers as a dedicated clinician.</en>
              <zh>古巴长笛演奏家、音乐教育家 Joel Fabelo 拥有逾二十年国际交响乐团与独奏舞台的深厚积淀。他的演奏风格兼具严谨的古典功底与自由热烈的加勒比律动，以精湛技巧横跨交响室内乐与现代拉丁音乐。如今，他频繁领衔迈阿密顶级拉丁乐团登台献艺，同时作为管乐导师与大师班专家，持续推动当代木管室内乐的发展。</zh>
            </bio>
          </performer>
        </performers>
      </item>
